  "definitions": {
    "coverage": "Share of the train catalog that appears in at least one top-k list. Point estimate only: a user bootstrap of this set-union is biased low and does not contain the point estimate (ADR-0003).",
    "intra_list_diversity": "Mean over users of 1 minus the mean pairwise cosine similarity of the top-k items. The item vector is the genre multi-hot from movies.dat.",
    "long_tail_share": "Mean over users of the fraction of the top-k list that falls in the train tail. The tail is every train item outside the top 20% head.",
    "mean_popularity": "Existing diagnostic: mean over users of the mean train interaction count of the top-k items. Not a second popularity metric.",
    "ndcg": "Existing binary NDCG@k (relevant when the test rating is at least the harness threshold). Recomputed on the lists scored here.",
    "novelty": "Mean over users of the mean self-information of the top-k items. Self-information of item i is -log2(count(i) / n_train_interactions), where count(i) is the number of train rows for i."
